  "reasoning": "Step 1: Identify key symptoms -> The patient reports swelling in the legs that causes difficulty fitting into shoes and discomfort when sitting for long periods. Step 2: Evaluate against possible diagnoses -> Leg swelling (edema) combined with discomfort exacerbated by prolonged sitting or standing is a hallmark of venous insufficiency and varicose veins, where pooled blood increases pressure in the lower extremities. Step 3: Rule out alternatives -> Diabetes typically presents with polyuria, polydipsia, and fatigue; hypertension with headaches and dizziness; arthritis with joint pain and stiffness. None of these align with the isolated leg swelling and sitting-related discomfort described. Step 4: Cross-reference with training data -> Multiple reference cases (e.g., cases 1, 3, 16, 19) explicitly link leg swelling, shoe-tightness, and discomfort from prolonged sitting/standing directly to varicose veins. Conclusion: The clinical picture and reference evidence firmly establish varicose veins as the correct diagnosis.",
  "final_answer": "[DIAGNOSIS]varicose veins[/DIAGNOSIS]"
}
